  "worked_solution": "First, we determine $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{(-1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17} \\\\  & =4.123\\,10\u2026 \\\\  & \u22484.12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute the reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{R} & =|\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =|\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(\\frac{-1}{4})| \\\\  & =|\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(-0.25)| \\\\  & =|-0.244\\,97\u2026| \\\\  & \u22480.244\\,97\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the point lies in the fourth quadrant, we subtract the reference angle from $2\\pi ,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta  & =2\\pi -{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =2\\pi -0.244\\,97 \\\\  & \u22486.04\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the polar coordinates of $P$ are $(4.12,6.04),$ rounded to two decimal places.",
